{"id": "EUVD-2026-48582", "enisaUuid": "87f9a801-0d01-3a4d-98d6-ce4f94c57f5e", "description": "DOMPurify before 3.4.12 fails to execute afterSanitizeElements hook for custom elements allowed via CUSTOM_ELEMENT_HANDLING.tagNameCheck, allowing attributes to bypass application security policies. Attackers can preserve sensitive attributes on custom elements that later re-inject them into innerHTML sinks, creating second-order XSS gadgets.", "datePublished": "2026-07-24T12:07:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T17:54:37", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify/security/advisories/GHSA-c2j3-45gr-mqc4", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dompurify-before-hook-bypass-via-custom-element-handling"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jxrp-r7gx-q4j8", "CVE-2026-66010"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a6a01f95-9fd4-3805-93e0-32cec1c11257", "product": {"name": "DOMPurify", "vendor": {"name": "cure53"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.4.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ceacf55f-60c6-35a7-95e3-0304183235d9", "vendor": {"name": "cure53"}}], "isExploited": false}